    }
  },
  "notes": {
    "Round/list": "An account update, then two instruction patches from one transaction: the second seq sorts below the first and the third equals it, yet each version is newer, so all apply.",
    "Event/list": "Each patch is routed to both subscriptions of the view and arrives twice with one version. Each applies once, so the appends do not double, and the second patch applies although its seq equals the first's.",
    "Pool/list": "A frame already in the snapshot arrives after it with a newer seq but an older version, and is dropped.",
    "Vault/list": "A new epoch is not compared with the old one: its first frame applies although its counter is lower. The same frame arriving again is a duplicate in that epoch, so its append applies once.",
    "Legacy/list": "Without versions the seq rule applies as before: the older seq is dropped."
  }
}
